2.0.1:
[Change] sshd rule expanded from 3 to 8 patterns: keyboard-interactive, ident
      string, refused connect, max auth attempts, PAM failure (LFD/fail2ban)
[Change] dovecot rule expanded from 2 to 5 patterns: Disconnected pop3/imap,
      submission-login auth failed
[Change] proftpd rule expanded from 1 to 4 patterns: incorrect password,
      SECURITY VIOLATION, maximum login attempts
[Change] exim_authfail rule expanded from 1 to 3 patterns: dovecot_*
      authenticator, SMTP protocol synchronization error
[Change] asterisk_badauth rule expanded from 1 to 2 patterns: SecurityEvent
      FailedACL (Asterisk 12+ security framework)
[Change] postfix PORTS updated from 25,26 to 25,26,587,465 (submission/SMTPS)
[Change] sendmail rule expanded from 1 to 2 patterns: AUTH failure
[New] tests/regex_samples.txt: 72-sample data-driven test corpus covering all
      34 rules with positive and negative test cases; RFC 5737 IP compliant;
      data-driven BATS tests in 13-regex-samples.bats validate all samples
      automatically (824 tests total)
[Change] conf.bfd restructured into workflow-oriented sections (Detection
      Thresholds, Email Alerts, Banning, Custom Firewall Commands, Log Paths,
      Advanced); comments rewritten to explain behavior; repeat-offender
      pipeline (BAN_ESCALATION/CAP + BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER/WINDOW) grouped with
      scenario examples; BAN_ESCALATION value "exponential" renamed to "double"
      (old value still accepted); 4 internal-only variables (LOCK_FILE_TIMEOUT,
      OUTPUT_SYSLOG_FILE, BAN_RETRY_COUNT, LOG_SOURCE) moved to internals.conf
      with backward-compatible defaults
[New] bfd.lib.sh: 112-function library extracted from bfd for testability
[New] extract_hosts() declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST>
      patterns, dual IPv4/IPv6 boundary-aware regex, and IGNOREREGEX per-rule
      exclusion; all 34 rules converted from ad-hoc grep/sed/awk pipelines
[New] 14 new service rules (34 total): apache-auth, nginx-http-auth,
      mysqld-auth, wordpress, webmin, directadmin, cyrus-imap, roundcube,
      plesk, dropbear, http_401, pam_generic, named, postgresql
[New] thresholds.conf: centralized per-rule threshold management (TRIG,
      SKIP_ALERT, RULE_EMAIL); three-tier precedence: rule file >
      thresholds.conf > conf.bfd
[New] _rule_tlog() in-process tlog wrapper replaces $TLOG_PATH subprocess in
      all 34 rules; eliminates 34 fork+exec pairs per detection cycle
[New] time-windowed failure counting via events.dat with TRIG_WINDOW (default
      300s) sliding window; TRIG_GLOBAL cross-service aggregate threshold
[New] distributed attack detection: SUBNET_TRIG unique IPs from same subnet
      triggers subnet ban; ip_to_subnet() with configurable IPv4/IPv6 masks
[New] FIREWALL="auto" with 8 backends (APF, CSF, firewalld, UFW, nftables,
      iptables, route, custom); auto-detection in priority order;
      fw_ban/fw_unban/fw_setup/fw_status dispatch layer; nftables sets,
      iptables chain, firewalld rich rules, route blackhole
[New] full IPv6 support: dual-stack detection, banning, and local address
      exclusion; BAN_COMMAND_V6/UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 for firewalls requiring
      separate commands; validate_ip6() with zone ID stripping
[New] temporary bans with auto-expiry (BAN_DURATION, default 300s); recidivism
      escalation (BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER/WINDOW); ban escalation modes
      (BAN_ESCALATION: none/linear/double, BAN_ESCALATION_CAP);
      execute_ban/execute_unban with retry and exponential backoff
[New] bans.active and bans.history state files with atomic flock -x appends;
      $PORTS substitution for port-specific blocking
[New] batched email alerts: single email per recipient per check cycle with
      enriched content (ban type, duration, recidivism, log excerpts);
      RULE_EMAIL per-rule routing; SKIP_ALERT per-rule suppression
[New] CLI expanded from 4 to 21 flags: -S/--status, -C/--config, -R/--rules,
      -T/--test, --test-pattern, -l/--list, -u/--unban, -b/--ban, -c/--check,
      -d/--dryrun, -w/--watch, -V/--verbose, -v/--version, -h/--help,
      --flush-temp, --flush-all, --json, --csv
[New] -w/--watch continuous daemon mode (WATCH_INTERVAL, default 10s); SIGHUP
      config reload; bfd-watch.service (systemd) and bfd-watch.init (SysVinit
      for CentOS 6 / Ubuntu 14.04); dead-PID lock recovery for cron fallback
[New] -V/--verbose flag with vout() instrumentation across check, unbans,
      status, and health check
[New] -c/--check health check: validates config, log paths, firewall binaries,
      rule status, state directories, tlog, and active bans
[New] detect_run_mode() for structured run-mode identification (watch/systemd,
      watch/init, watch/manual, timer/systemd, cron, unknown)
[New] systemd journal reader with transparent fallback (16 of 34 rules);
      LOG_SOURCE config (auto/file/journal); cursor-based journal tracking
[New] conf.bfd reorganized into 6 sections; internals.conf split out;
      validate_config() checks 24 variables at startup with clear error
      messages and meaningful exit codes
[New] bfd.1 nroff man page (OPTIONS, CONFIGURATION, THRESHOLDS, FIREWALL,
      RULES, FILES, SIGNALS, EXIT CODES); installed via install.sh
[New] bfd.bash-completion: context-sensitive tab completion for all CLI flags,
      IPs, rule names, config variables, and file paths
[New] importconf rewritten: awk-based config merge preserving user values;
      thresholds.conf migration; pre-2.0.1 backward compat (FIREWALL=
      "custom"); temp file cleanup trap
[New] install.sh: custom paths (INSTALL_PATH/BIN_PATH env vars); man page,
      bash completion, and SysVinit init script installation; post-install
      watch mode recommendation; stats/ mkdir
[New] uninstall.sh: root check; service stop ordering; man page, completion,
      init script, and backup directory cleanup
[New] safe_source() validates root ownership and non-world-writable permissions
      before sourcing; expand_command_template() and sanitize_ports() for safe
      template expansion without eval
[New] validate_ip()/validate_ip6()/validate_ip_any() strict IP validation;
      sanitize_mod() restricts rule names to safe characters
[New] record_ban(), _save/_restore/_clear_rule_vars(), _rule_is_active()
      helpers consolidating duplicated logic across callers
[New] bfd.service, bfd.timer, bfd-watch.service systemd units with
      SyslogIdentifier
[New] .shellcheckrc and full shellcheck compliance across all scripts
[New] .github/workflows/ci.yml with 8-OS Docker matrix and Buildx caching
[New] BATS test suite: 819 tests across 29 .bats files; shared helpers
      (assert-bfd.bash, bfd-mock.bash, bfd-common.bash); parallel runner;
      9 Dockerfiles; RFC 5737 test IPs throughout
[Change] check() refactored: delegates to filter_host/count_failures/
         execute_ban; skips already-banned hosts; per-run statistics;
         duplicate-ban prevention via state_bans_active_check()
[Change] tlog modernized: cat subprocesses → read builtin; getsize() pre-
         create block eliminated (prevents double-read race); growth condition
         simplified; convergence with tlog_read() documented
[Change] shell modernization across all files: backticks → $(), $[expr] →
         $(( )), egrep → grep -E, for-cat → while-read, systematic variable
         quoting, hardcoded paths → command -v discovery
[Change] -a/--attackpool extended with search_ip() report, per-service
         breakdown, and ban status integration
[Change] logrotate.d.bfd rewritten: copytruncate, weekly, compress, create 0640
[Change] cron.daily: flock-wrapped state rotation; copy-and-truncate preserves
         inodes; INSTALL_PATH variable; cursor files preserved; GPL header added
[Change] README wholesale rewrite: quick start, config reference, rule catalog,
         ban lifecycle, firewall backends, IPv6, CLI flags, troubleshooting
[Change] default cron interval reduced from 3 to 2 minutes
[Change] version 1.6-1 → 2.0.1; copyright years updated to 2026
[Fix] security: alert eval echo injection replaced with expand_command_
      template(); show_config() eval injection guarded by whitelist;
      BAN_COMMAND template extracted raw preventing premature expansion;
      custom backend PORTS validated via sanitize_ports()
[Fix] security: safe_source() applied to all sourced files (bfd.lib.sh,
      conf.bfd, alert.bfd, rules, tlog); state file operations wrapped in
      flock -x; mktemp replaces PID-based temp files; state files created 600;
      tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat
[Fix] global lock: FD-based flock replaced with mkdir-based lock eliminating
      eval "exec $LOCK_FD" and fd-0-close risk; PID liveness check clears dead
      holder immediately for cron recovery
[Fix] install.sh: daemon-reload after sed; BINPATH parent dir creation; CWD
      portability; chmod 640 for sourced files via find -type f; stats/ mkdir
      with chmod 750; no-op sed target removed
[Fix] validate_config(): added OUTPUT_SYSLOG, EMAIL_ADDRESS, BFD_LOG_PATH,
      BAN_RETRY_COUNT, EMAIL_LOGLINES validation; header comment updated
[Fix] show_config(): BAN_COMMAND vars added to whitelist with _TEMPLATE mapping
[Fix] rule variable leakage: IGNOREREGEX/PORTS/SKIP_ALERT/RULE_EMAIL now
      properly reset between rules via _clear/_save/_restore helpers
[Fix] CLI exit codes: all dispatch branches validate args and propagate via
      || exit "$?"; unknown flags exit non-zero
[Fix] firewall backends: hardcoded paths replaced with command -v discovery
      for apf, csf, iptables, ip6tables, ip (route backend); CIDR addresses
      pass through without extra /32 or /128 suffix
[Fix] tlog: log rotation duplicate output; source safety validation;
      indentation normalized; idioms and version string updated
[Fix] rule fixes: postgresql impossible path test; vsftpd2 TLOG_TF collision;
      modsec FILE→LP rename; missing SKIP_ALERT in postfix/proftpd;
      ignore.hosts missing ::1 loopback
[Fix] IPv6: grep -Fw false-match replaced with awk/grep -Fx exact matching
[Fix] journal: tlog_journal_filter rh_ipop3d key mismatch; dispatch bypassed
      existing log files
[Fix] miscellaneous: POSIX == → = in [ ] tests; $EXIT_* quoting; _hc_config()
      eval → case; _apool_report() date -d fallback; -q subprocess → exec;
      attack pool regex → grep -F; local address grep -Ew fix; WATCH_INTERVAL
      ${-} → ${:-}; sed -r → sed -E; $! quoting; UNBAN_COMMAND warning gated
      on FIREWALL="custom"; firewalld examples removed --permanent flag
